From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:45:16 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] audio: spdif: keep a shared source pll at its rate on close

Closing a spdif output after a 44.1k stream sets hifi_pll back to the
48k rate. When hifi_pll is also the 44.1k source of another output, a
stream still playing there runs about 9% fast until its next setup.
---
 sound/soc/amlogic/auge/spdif.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/amlogic/auge/spdif.c b/sound/soc/amlogic/auge/spdif.c
--- a/sound/soc/amlogic/auge/spdif.c
+++ b/sound/soc/amlogic/auge/spdif.c
@@ -0,6 +0,10 @@
 
 	if (!clk_name)
 		return;
+	/* a pll that serves both rate families keeps the rate in use */
+	if (!IS_ERR(p_spdif->clk_src_cd) &&
+	    clk_is_match(p_spdif->sysclk, p_spdif->clk_src_cd))
+		return;
 	if (p_spdif->standard_sysclk % 11025 == 0) {
 		if (!strcmp(__clk_get_name(clk_get_parent(p_spdif->clk_spdifout)),
 				__clk_get_name(p_spdif->sysclk))) {
